      "takeaway": "Europe's wealthiest nations are recording unprecedented summer death tolls from heat, revealing that existing prevention systems are failing even in countries with advanced medical capacity.",
      "why_it_matters": "The scale of heat-related deaths across major European economies—14,000 in Germany and 4,500 in Spain in a single summer—exposes the lethal vulnerability of Europe's healthcare and public health infrastructure to extreme temperatures, raising urgent questions about preparation and coordination across the continent."
